Dear MaAsLin users,

One year ago (December 2017), I run MaAsLin to compare gut microbial pathways between 2 patient groups (MaAsLin run 1).

Then a year later (December 2018), I rerun this MaAsLin analysis (MaAsLin run 2), and – although the metadata and microbiome abundance input files used by MaAsLin are exactly equal – the output file is completely different.

When going through the log files of MaAsLin run 1 and 2, it seems that MaAsLin performs a different covariate selection for the model. Link to log files: https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1-BUHtkcpzyvJOHpUtKVjj0DbVADPyvaA?usp=sharing. Do you think that the different output files from MaAsLin run 1 and 2, could be explained by differences in MaAsLin/package versions?

Thank you in advance,

Kind regards,

Marjolein Klaassen

MD/PhD-student

Gastroenterology and Hepatology Department

Universitiy Medical Center Groningen

The Netherlands

